{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nNow I have a clear picture of the bug and all the artifacts. Let me summarize the analysis, then implement everything.\n\n**Bug analysis**: `_normalize_requested_path` only calls `unquote()` once, so double-encoded paths like `%252e%252e%252fsecrets.csv` → `%2e%2e%2fsecrets.csv` bypass the `..` substring check. The `..` check is also substring-based rather than component-based, which is fragile.\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nSkipping the plan tool due to parsing issues. Let me proceed directly with the fix.\n\n**Bug root cause**: `_normalize_requested_path` only calls `unquote()` once. Double-encoded paths like `%252e%252e%252f` → `%2e%2e%2f` (after one decode) never become `../`, so the `..` substring check is bypassed. The fix: decode repeatedly until stable, then check `..` as a path component (not substring).\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /workspace/repo/export_api/storage.py << 'PYEOF'\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import unquote\n\n\nclass ExportPathViolation(ValueError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef _normalize_requested_path(requested_path: str) -> str:\n    if not isinstance(requested_path, str) or not requested_path:\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"requested_path must be a non-empty string\\\")\n    normalized = unquote(requested_path).replace(\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\"/\\\")\n    # Repeatedly decode until stable to catch double/multi-encoding\n    prev = \\\"\\\"\n    while prev \"'!= normalized:\n        prev = normalized\n        normalized = unquote(normalized)\n    normalized = normalized.replace(\"'\"\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\"/\\\").lstrip(\\\"/\\\")\n    while \\\"//\\\" in normalized:\n        normalized = normalized.replace(\\\"//\\\", \\\"/\\\")\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef resolve_export_path(tenant_root: Path, requested_path: str) -> Path:\n    normalized = _normalize_requested_path(requested_path)\n    if normalized.startswith(\\\"/\\\"):\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"blocked suspicious export path\\\")\n    parts = normalized.split(\\\"/\\\")\n    if any(part == \\\"..\\\" for part in parts):\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"blocked suspicious export path\\\")\n    candidate = (tenant_root / normalized).resolve(strict=False)\n    if not str(candidate).startswith(str(tenant_root.resolve())):\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"candidate escaped the tenant root\\\")\n    return candidate\nPYEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
